Been playing NH for about a year and a half now. I've ascended many
times, including several pacifists (healers and a gnome wiz) and
illiterates (all Tourists), but this was the first time I've tried
combining those conducts. This game (like the majority of NH games I
play) was on NAO - dumplog is here -
http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/e/edmu52c/dumplog/1328776802.nh343.txt.

I was really lucky in the early game - found a stethoscope in a large
general store on Dlvl 3, managed to make it through the Mines at XL 1,
and got to Minetown. Temple was coaligned so I bought protection and
alignment, and got a magic whistle and leash from the tool shop.

Then I went on to Sokoban...fairly uneventful, aside from my pets
almost getting killed by the giant mimics...and after getting the BoH
there I returned  to my Minetown stash and continue further down the
Mines. I managed to to find a polytrap (3 actually, though 2 of them I
found by stepping in them myself, thus leaving only 1) and eventually
polyed my pets into an Olog-hai and an elvenking (which later ate a
chameleon corpse and became another Olog-hai). At this point it was
pretty easy, so I just continued exploring - stumbled across the
Portal for Ludios while digging for vaults - I let my pets kill the
soldiers though as I had no MR or reflection I wasn't about to step
into the courtyard where the dragons were, so I just left there after
the soldiers were dead...at least I got a bugle, which allowed me to
open the Castle bridge. Clearing the Castle was pretty uneventful,
aside from an air E that engulfed me several times...

After using the Castle wand (fortunately it was (0:3)) to wish for the
Eyes, the Orb of Fate, and SDSM, I levelported back to my stash in
Minetown to sort out all the stuff I'd just gotten at the Castle, and
went back to the Castle to farm the throne for potions, mainly for
gain level. After a while this got tiresome, so I went back to my
stash to wish for an Archon figurine with the magic lamp I'd found in
the Valley, and try some random alchemy - dipping water into object
detection eventually netted me 22 potions of gain level, enough to get
myself to XL 14 and have enough left over to (after having also picked
up a few more potions in Gehennom later on) get my Archon to level 49.

I went through the Quest, then did some polypiling (found a polywand
on the Quest) and ended up with 28 scrolls of scare monster, a
levitation ring, can of grease, and a few more candles (probably a
couple other rings/tools...don't recall exactly...).

Then I just started going through Gehennom, with my Archon, 2 Olog-
hai, and a purple worm I'd picked up at some point. Also, somewhere
along the way I managed to wish up a magic harp and frost horn (I
think a throne on the quest, and another magic lamp). I found a random
wand of wishing in Orcustown, but didn't really need it so I just used
it for wishing up a +5 shield of reflection for my Archon (reduce AC
to minimize chance of getting gulped by a purple worm, plus ensure it
wouldn't swap reflection for some +4 shield or something from some
random soldier it happened to kill...).

Waking Rodney, performing the Invocation, strolling through the
Sanctum, and running back up with the Amulet were all pretty
uneventful - no major summon storms - Rodney did Double Trouble a few
times, and summoned nasties occasionally, but my pets made quick work
of whatever was there, though my Olog-hai both eventually got killed
while still in Gehennom.

The Planes were similarly trivial - no further appearances by Rodney,
beyond the guaranteed one on Earth - and Astral was a breeze with my
magic harp + tele wands, plus the coaligned temple happened to be the
first one I visited. I probably could've kept going around Astral like
I would usually do, collecting artifacts and other goodies from player
monsters, but I decided not to take (many) chances and just used up a
few wishes for pointless junk, just because I could, then offered the
Amulet.


